  "name": "audio-tail",
  "note": "Audio probe. 3D67 is the last unknown whose meaning is audible rather than visible: 802176A8 routes numbers below 11 through jump table 8021F058 to pick a track. In the original scripts it appears in two fixed shapes — 3D4E then 3D67 n then 3D38 then 3D45 <group> (right before reinforcements arrive) and 3D54 145, 3D35, 3D67 0, 3D5C 145,1 (right before Combattler V combines) — so it reads as a fanfare for a dramatic entrance. All four original values 0/1/3/4 are probed, each bracketed by silence (3D3A 0) so the capture attributes sound to one command, with a known BGM (3D3A 49) at the start as a positive control. Run with --audio and SRW64_AUDIO_CAPTURE_FROM/_TO around the probe span. audio-2 reorders the probes so 3D75/3D68/3D36/3D63 come first and fit inside one capture window; the four 3D67 runs are long enough to push them past any reasonable window otherwise.",
